- Test data seeding and database isolation
- Mocking external services (email delivery, OIDC sign-in)
- Assertions for UI state and created resources
- Time-bounded test design for CI/CD pipelines

## Code Example

```javascript
// Using Playwright
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('complete onboarding flow', async ({ page }) => {
  // Seed deterministic test data
  await seedTestUser({ email: 'demo@test.com', password: 'Test123!' });

  // Mock email service to capture verification link
  await mockEmailService();

  // Mock OIDC provider
  await mockOIDCProvider();

  // Navigate to signup and complete registration
  await page.goto('/signup');
  await page.fill('[name=email]', 'demo@test.com');
  await page.fill('[name=password]', 'Test123!');
  await page.click('[data-testid=signup-submit]');

  // Extract and follow email verification link
  const verifyLink = await getVerificationLink('demo@test.com');
  await page.goto(verifyLink);

  // Complete profile setup
  await page.fill('[name=name]', 'Jane Doe');
  await page.fill('[name=company]', 'Acme Corp');
  await page.click('[data-testid=profile-submit]');

  // Create first workspace
  await page.fill('[name=workspaceName]', 'My Workspace');
  await page.click('[data-testid=create-workspace]');

  // Assert dashboard displays new workspace
  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid=workspace-card]')).toContainText('My Workspace');
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Offline-first reliability with service workers is a critical requirement in modern e-commerce applications. This question evaluates whether a candidate understands how to test caching behavior, connectivity state changes, and retry logic in end-to-end tests.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first UX patterns with service workers
- Network throttling and failure simulation (Cypress or Playwright network interception)
- Test data isolation with fixtures or unique identifiers
- Idempotent order placement to prevent duplicate charges

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Intercept network requests to simulate offline behavior
cy.intercept('POST', '/api/payment', (req) => {
  req.reply({ statusCode: 503, body: { error: 'Network error' } });
}).as('paymentRequest');

// Simulate going offline
cy.networkIdle(); // or use Cypress offline plugin
cy.window().then((win) => {
  win.navigator.onLine = false;
});

// Verify offline UI and localStorage persistence
cy.get('[data-testid=offline-banner]').should('be.visible');
cy.getLocalStorage('cart').should('exist');

// Restore network and retry
cy.networkOn();
cy.wait('@paymentRequest').then(() => {
  cy.get('[data-testid=order-confirmation]').should('be.visible');
});

// Verify idempotent order creation
cy.get('@paymentRequest').its('response.statusCode').should('eq', 200);
```

